From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:04:02 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 22/37] Plutonium: Chrome's own UI in the shell (DevTools,
 context menus, keys)

In shell mode the page is the desktop, so Chrome's browser-window UI
stays out of it (EXO-CHROME):

- DevTools: a shell's window docks its page's DevTools at the side. A
  shell tab's DevTools, with no browser window to dock in, becomes a tab
  of its own (opened by "devtools", the inspected tab's tags) that the
  shell shows beside it; it can't be navigated or automated. Shell tabs
  are "page" DevTools targets.
- Context menus: a shell page's and a tab's menu lose the browser-window
  items (Cast, Print, Save as, Inspect, Exit full screen, ...). The
  visible shell gets them as navigator.windowBroker's cancelable
  "contextmenurequest" and answers with closeContextMenu(); otherwise
  Chrome shows its own, filtered. Reload works in tabs.
- Keys: a shell's window runs only DevTools and clipboard commands (no F1
  help window, Ctrl+N, Ctrl+W closing the shell, ...). Tabs get DevTools
  keys, Alt+Left/Right and F5/Ctrl+R. Of Ash's accelerators only hardware
  keys stay (no UI scaling on Ctrl+Shift+plus, IME switching on
  Ctrl+Space, clipboard history on Search+V, accessibility toggles).
- No link status bubble.

